cue-y0quet1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:06.000
What is the volume of a cube
whose side is a plus b?

cue-cemp3w2
00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:11.500
Cut every side into two parts:
a, and b.

cue-dqo5863
00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:17.680
Cut along those parts,
and the cube falls into eight blocks.

cue-r4x1pg4
00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:22.630
The blocks come in four kinds.

cue-3y2ijd5
00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:29.780
Put like with like. First, one cube
with side a: a cubed.

cue-ijt83s6
00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:36.080
Next, three slabs, each a by a by b:
three a squared b.

cue-zpdk117
00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:42.480
Then three bars, each a by b by b:
three a b squared.

cue-rgxjxb8
00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:47.850
And one small cube with side b:
b cubed.

cue-h9il8j9
00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:56.800
So a plus b, cubed, equals a cubed, plus three a squared b,
plus three a b squared, plus b cubed.

cue-ubpkbua
00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.800
